Z||000000||84se48||05-20-2001||05:23 PM||||Took car out for test ride,engine light came on, looked down at dash an saw speedometer sitting on zip! took my foot off gas, light went off an speedometer started moving.Its boncing all over the place. At slow speed it does nothing. Is there something wrong with it or a sensor?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||05-20-2001||06:49 PM||||Two things come to mind...<BR>sensor/sender, or ECM...<BR>Hope it's the sender...<BR>crash...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||KissMySSFiero||05-20-2001||09:16 PM||||this happened to me.  it wasnt the sender.  check the wires coming out of the sender.  with a 17 year old car the wires tend to get brittle.  or the clips that hold them up break.  well the way the wires arer routed in the engine bay.  if they fall they get rubbed against the axle.  mine did this same thing and all it was is that the wire had rubbed thru the insulation and broke.  so i spliced the wire and reconnected it.  worked like new.  hope this can help.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">          <BR>"When in Doubt..Whip it out!!"||||reg||1
